title: 'Michael Nygard, "Documenting Architecture Decisions" (2011): without the reasons, a newcomer can only blindly accept a decision or blindly change it.'
pid: e9270901-cf61-4a35-bac3-c83839256b4f
body: |2-
  https://cognitect.com/blog/2011/11/15/documenting-architecture-decisions
  Each record: title, context, decision ("We will ..."), status,
  consequences; one or two pages; one significant decision each;
  kept in the repository; reversed decisions are kept and marked
  superseded. Written as a conversation with a future developer.
  Every mind on this team is that newcomer, every mission.
